💬 Viva Questions and Answers
Question	Answer
What is a struct in Solidity?	A custom data type to group related data under one name.
Why use arrays in smart contracts?	To store multiple similar records dynamically.
What is the difference between receive() and fallback()?	receive() is used for plain Ether transfers; fallback() is used when unknown function or data is sent.
What does external keyword mean?	Function can be called from outside the contract.
What is payable?	Allows the function/contract to send or receive Ether.
What is emit used for?	To trigger an event and log information on the blockchain.
What happens if Ether is sent to a contract without receive() or fallback()?	The transaction fails and Ether is reverted.
What is the meaning of Gas in Ethereum?	Gas measures the computational effort required to execute operations on the Ethereum network.
Why are read-only functions (view) free in Remix?	They do not modify blockchain state; hence, no gas is consumed.
What is a test network?	A network used for testing smart contracts (e.g., Sepolia, Goerli) using fake Ether.
